WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.167
-Former President Donald Trump

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.934
praised Vladimir Putin's savvy
and genius

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.901
amid U.S. warnings
of an imminent

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.434
full-scale Russian invasion
of Ukraine,

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:10.968
and yet even as
he was doing that,

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:13.567
Republicans and right-wing
pundits claimed

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.801
it was President Biden
who was showing weakness.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.100
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.767
I do not profess to be
a foreign policy expert

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:25.767
by any stretch.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.834
Most of my
foreign policy experience

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.968
comes from my magical
semester abroad in Rome

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.801
when I dodged
out-of-control Vespas

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.300
and fell in
with Dickie Greenleaf

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.434
and that creep Tom Ripley.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.601
And, oh, wait, that's a movie.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:37.701
I'm remembering a movie.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:40.501
Anyway, I'm no
foreign policy expert,

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:43.334
but even I can see that
virtually no one in the world

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.434
thinks what Russia is doing
right now is a good idea --

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:48.133
apparently, not even
Putin's own advisers,

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.834
who looked frozen and terrified

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:52.067
during a bizarre
National Security meeting

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.601
broadcast on Russian television
earlier this week,

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.634
where Putin quizzed them
one by one

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:59.501
on what he should do as if he
didn't already know the answers.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:03.501
-The National Security Council
of Russia had a televised event.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:06.434
They broadcast this
highly choreographed session

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.367
of the Security Council
in Russia,

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.367
in which they were discussing
the possibility,

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.300
Vladimir Putin
and his top officials,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.567
of recognizing those rebel
republics in the east of Ukraine

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.200
as independent states.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.267
-This was when he was speaking
to his Security Council

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.367
before the actual address
to the nation, to be clear.

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:24.868
And according to
the Moscow bureau chief

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.267
of the "Financial Times,"
these are --

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.200
well, we know these the
senior-most Russian officials

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.734
over there sort of arrayed.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:33.300
None of them were within
20 yards of Putin at any point.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.834
-First of all, why is he sitting
so far away from them?

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:39.067
Did he put them there,
or did they all gradually

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:41.734
scoot their chairs back
during the meeting?

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.167
[ Russian accent ]
Yes, Mr. President,

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:47.133
in regards to Ukraine,
I believe best path forward,

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.701
and don't --
don't quote me on this,

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:53.968
because I would like very much
not to be wrong.

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.033
[ Normal voice ] Usually to see
people sit that far away,

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:59.701
a guy has to bring
a Komodo dragon onto the subway.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:01.634
"Hey, don't worry, everybody,
he doesn't bite.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:05.734
Ow! Bad timing, Gary."

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:06.934
This photo --

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:11.801
This photo reminds me
of an interview Trump did

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:14.701
during the 2020 campaign
at the Lincoln Memorial

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.067
when the interviewers sat
like a mile away from him.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.133
I guess they wanted
to be far enough away

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.000
so they could get up
and leave at any moment

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.100
without Trump noticing,
you know, just sneak off

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.601
during one of his insane rants.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:25.901
[ As Trump ]
Lincoln, we love Lincoln.

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:27.167
Good old Abe.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.601
"Abe" rhymes with "Gabe,"
which, of course,

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:31.734
reminds me of the great --
the great Gabe Kaplan.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.234
He should -- He should really

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.601
have a statue, too,
if you ask me.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.801
Welcome back, Kotter.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.934
Kotter.
He left, but he came back.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.501
He came back.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.133
He came back and he whipped
those Sweathogs into shape.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:46.067
Oh, we love the Sweathogs,
don't we, folks?

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.868
We love -- Folks?

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:50.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:52.400
[ Normal voice ] I'm pretty sure
that once Trump got rolling,

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.133
even Lincoln scooched
his chair back a little.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.000
[ Rumbling ]

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.567
Really good.

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:06.033
Guys, this is the first time
we see the graphics, too, so...

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:09.801
If a single tear
rolls down my face,

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:11.601
just know it's 'cause
I'm really [bleep] proud

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.801
of what they did today.

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.667
Also, check out this close-up
of Putin's advisers.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:19.701
Yikes!
They look like they're all

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:21.601
in the waiting room
for a colonoscopy.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.667
You know things are bleak
when even Putin's closest

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.934
and most loyal advisers don't
want to look him in the eye.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:29.300
That's the way my staff
looks at me when I say,

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.467
"I think I might do my
Al Pacino impression tonight.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.100
What do you think, Mikhail?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.167
Mikhail?

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.801
Should I do the Pacino?

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.400
Barb?

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.567
Barb, you're looking
like you think

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.901
the Pacino might
be a good idea."

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:46.601
Yeah, but you know what?
Maybe it won't work.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.434
I mean, because tonight's
"Closer Look" is about --

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:51.067
[ As Pacino ] Ukraine.
Our crane.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:54.267
This whole courtroom is crane.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.167
[ Normal voice ]
See, the audience loves it.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:59.300
How about you, Lincoln?
You love it, right?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.834
[ Rumbling ]

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:05.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:08.534
And just to give you an idea
of how nervous and reticent

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:11.133
even Putin's closest advisers
have been to agree with him,

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.901
at one point, Putin demanded

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:15.267
that the director of Russia's
Foreign Intelligence Service

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.000
give an opinion
about whether Putin

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.300
should recognize
two breakaway regions of Ukraine

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.234
as independent territories,
which, of course, he later did.

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:24.634
Here's how that exchange went,

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.767
according to a reporter
for the "Financial Times."

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:29.968
Putin said, "Speak clearly,
do you support recognition?"

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.667
And the adviser said, "I will."

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.834
To which Putin replied,
"You will or you do?"

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.033
Then the adviser said,

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:38.033
"I support bringing them
into Russia."

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:41.133
To which Putin replied, "That's
not what we are discussing.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:43.501
Do you support
recognizing independence?"

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:46.834
And then the adviser,
flustered, said, "Yes."

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.234
Jesus!

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:52.300
I have flop sweat
just from reading that exchange.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.767
Usually you got to dangle
a guy over a shark tank

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.300
to get that tense
a back-and-forth.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.100
And, Vlad, the last thing
I want to do

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.434
is give you management notes,

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:02.801
but the way you say things
like "speak clearly"

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.834
almost guarantees
that people won't.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.501
Hoo-ah!

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:22.601
So look, if their body language

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.634
and tentative responses
are any indication,

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.400
not even Putin's
closest advisers

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.100
thought this was
an especially smart move.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.400
Virtually no one does.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.901
The entire world is aghast
and horrified.

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.267
The only people
who could possibly think

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.968
this is a good move are those
unemployed fringe weirdos

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.534
who go on
small-time radio shows.

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:39.701
You know, like this guy.

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:26.834
No, you don't got to say that.

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:28.801
I mean, well,
maybe you got to say that

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:31.334
so someone will pick you up
at the Moscow airport

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:33.167
when you flee our jurisdiction.

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:35.901
It's just insane that Trump
is still so desperate

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:38.701
to praise a bloodthirsty tyrant
like Putin every chance he get.

00:06:38.701 --> 00:06:41.167
Trump narrates Putin's
every move like he's Tony Romo

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.000
calling the last drive
of a playoff game.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.033
"Oh, man, here he comes.

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:45.501
He's setting up
at the goal line.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:47.200
And he's going to roll tanks
into the end zone.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.234
You got to say, Jim,
this is very savvy."

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.367
Also, can we go back
to the beginning of that clip?

00:06:55.267 --> 00:07:00.400
Oh, there was a TV screen
in a room you went into.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.067
I guarantee you there's not
a room in that man's life

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.367
where there isn't a TV screen.

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:06.901
Even his sauna has a TV
with a squeegee next to it

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:08.834
to wipe off the condensation.

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.901 --> 00:07:13.467
[ As Trump ] Sean Hannity's
sweating again.

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:15.067
Oh, okay, okay.

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:18.567
[ Normal voice ] So Putin's
own advisers look scared.

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:21.133
Meanwhile, Trump's watching
Russian tanks roll into Ukraine

00:07:21.133 --> 00:07:23.567
with pom-poms in his hands,
calling it genius.

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:25.033
And in that story,

00:07:25.033 --> 00:07:27.934
who did he say the words
"this is genius" to, anyway?

00:07:27.934 --> 00:07:29.334
Was Melania
in the room with him?

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:31.901
[ As Trump ] Mel?
Mel, you got to come see --

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:34.601
Vlad's inva--
It's genius, Mel.

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:36.934
Mel? Mel.
Oh, wait a minute.

00:07:36.934 --> 00:07:40.200
This is just a scarecrow
with a dress on it.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.167
Well played, Mel.

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:44.701
[ Normal voice ] So the leader
of the Republican Party

00:07:44.701 --> 00:07:46.834
is calling lawless
Russian military aggression

00:07:46.834 --> 00:07:48.534
toward a sovereign country
genius,

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.734
while President Biden is trying
to unite world allies

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:52.133
to stop Russia

00:07:52.133 --> 00:07:55.067
and making it clear he does
not want a war with Russia.

00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:58.501
-Who in the Lord's name does
Putin think gives him the right

00:07:58.501 --> 00:08:02.367
to declare new
so-called countries

00:08:02.367 --> 00:08:05.200
on territory that belong
to his neighbors?

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:08.334
This is a flagrant violation
of international law

00:08:08.334 --> 00:08:11.634
and demands a firm response from
the international community.

00:08:11.634 --> 00:08:12.934
Let me be clear.

00:08:12.934 --> 00:08:16.334
These are totally defensive
moves on our part.

00:08:16.334 --> 00:08:19.434
We have no intention
of fighting Russia.

00:08:19.434 --> 00:08:21.000
-First of all, I'm glad
he said that last part,

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.667
since no one serious
seems to want

00:08:22.667 --> 00:08:24.133
or is suggesting a war
with Russia,

00:08:24.133 --> 00:08:26.267
which would be catastrophic,
which is why the world

00:08:26.267 --> 00:08:28.267
needs to do everything possible
to avoid one.

00:08:28.267 --> 00:08:30.400
Second, I like when Biden
goes full Scranton

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.167
and uses old-timey phrases
like "who in the Lord's name?"

00:08:34.167 --> 00:08:36.200
Biden's got the tone
of a guidance counselor

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.634
sitting backwards on a chair,

00:08:37.634 --> 00:08:41.200
trying to talk a burnout kid
into turning his life around.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.901
[ As Biden ] So you think you're
some hotshot, huh, chief?

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:48.033
Recognizing breakaway regions,
invading your neighbors.

00:08:48.033 --> 00:08:51.267
Who in the Lord's name
do you think you are?

00:08:51.267 --> 00:08:52.968
Guess what -- You're not
going cruisin' tonight,

00:08:52.968 --> 00:08:55.234
'cause you're in detention
with the rest of the Sweathogs.

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.067 --> 00:08:59.901
[ Normal voice ]
And yet in comparing those two
reactions from Trump and Biden,

00:08:59.901 --> 00:09:02.434
Republicans apparently come to
the obviously insane conclusion

00:09:02.434 --> 00:09:05.267
that it was Biden who was
somehow projecting weakness,

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:07.267
although Biden's critics
on the right

00:09:07.267 --> 00:09:08.667
can't seem to make up
their minds

00:09:08.667 --> 00:09:11.133
about whether we should be
showing strength toward Putin

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:14.000
or whether we should just
be siding with Putin.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.067
-The administration,
basically on the Obama model,

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:19.434
is for weakness.

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:20.968
They avoid war, frankly,

00:09:20.968 --> 00:09:23.434
by accepting surrender
of their own interests.

00:09:23.434 --> 00:09:25.434
-The GOP House conference
tweeted a picture of Biden

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:27.200
walking away from the podium
with this quote --

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.868
"This is what weakness
on the world stage looks like."

00:09:29.868 --> 00:09:31.934
-The administration
has been so muddled

00:09:31.934 --> 00:09:34.567
in the way they have
made Vladimir Putin

00:09:34.567 --> 00:09:36.968
have the upper hand
throughout this entire time.

00:09:36.968 --> 00:09:39.934
-The White House,
it seems like the response,

00:09:39.934 --> 00:09:42.534
even though it was supposed to
be quite robust, was very timid.

00:09:42.534 --> 00:09:45.734
-He looks very weak, and Russia
is taking advantage of it.

00:09:45.734 --> 00:09:46.901
-It might be worth
asking yourself,

00:09:46.901 --> 00:09:48.667
since it is getting
pretty serious,

00:09:48.667 --> 00:09:50.000
"What is this really about?

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.467
Why do I hate Putin so much?

00:09:52.467 --> 00:09:54.300
Has Putin ever called me
a racist?

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.501
Has he threatened to get me
fired for disagreeing with him?

00:09:57.501 --> 00:09:59.167
Has he shipped
every middle-class job

00:09:59.167 --> 00:10:00.901
in my town to Russia?

00:10:00.901 --> 00:10:03.000
Did he manufacture
a worldwide pandemic

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.033
that wrecked my business and
kept me indoors for two years?

00:10:06.033 --> 00:10:09.467
Is he teaching my children to
embrace racial discrimination?

00:10:09.467 --> 00:10:11.033
Is he making fentanyl?

00:10:11.033 --> 00:10:12.868
Is he trying
to snuff out Christianity?

00:10:12.868 --> 00:10:14.601
Does he eat dogs?"

00:10:14.601 --> 00:10:18.434
-Why? Why do I hate Putin
so much?

00:10:18.434 --> 00:10:19.567
Did he call me a racist?

00:10:19.567 --> 00:10:21.200
Did he get me fired from my job?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.701
Did he ring my doorbell
and run away,

00:10:22.701 --> 00:10:25.200
leaving a flaming paper bag
on my doorstep?

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.100
A bag I then stomped on,

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.667
only to discover it was filled
with dog feces?

00:10:29.667 --> 00:10:31.133
Did he make plans with me

00:10:31.133 --> 00:10:33.267
as means of an apology
for the dog [bleep] prank

00:10:33.267 --> 00:10:35.767
to meet at a fancy restaurant
and then not show up on time,

00:10:35.767 --> 00:10:39.100
texting every five minutes,
"On way, there soon,"

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:42.234
only to arrive an hour late and
then say, "I had a late lunch.

00:10:42.234 --> 00:10:44.767
Is it cool
if I just watch you eat?"

00:10:44.767 --> 00:10:47.901
And then when my food did come,
would he pick it off my plate,

00:10:47.901 --> 00:10:49.100
one French fry at a time,

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.634
until he'd eaten at least
half of the French fries?

00:10:51.634 --> 00:10:52.968
And when the bill
came from the waiter,

00:10:52.968 --> 00:10:55.100
did he point at me and say,
"I actually didn't eat"?

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:56.400
Even though both the waiter
and I

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.634
could see the giant
ketchup smudge on his face

00:10:58.634 --> 00:11:02.133
from the colossal bite
he took of my burger?

00:11:02.133 --> 00:11:05.067
Did Vladimir Putin
do that to me?

00:11:05.067 --> 00:11:06.334
Yes, he did.

00:11:06.334 --> 00:11:08.000
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.067
He did it yesterday.

00:11:10.067 --> 00:11:12.133
Also, to all those warmongers,

00:11:12.133 --> 00:11:13.567
like Mike Pompeo
and Newt Gingrich

00:11:13.567 --> 00:11:15.234
and the House Republicans
who called Biden weak,

00:11:15.234 --> 00:11:17.534
your dude is the one
who just called Putin savvy

00:11:17.534 --> 00:11:18.968
and praised his genius.

00:11:18.968 --> 00:11:20.734
Do you guys even pay attention
to what Trump is saying anymore?

00:11:20.734 --> 00:11:22.601
Or do you just assume,
like most of us,

00:11:22.601 --> 00:11:24.400
that he got lost
wandering around the 18th hole

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.133
at one of his golf courses and
now he just lives in a sand trap

00:11:27.133 --> 00:11:28.634
with a bunch of pigeons?

00:11:28.634 --> 00:11:30.067
And even when he was president,

00:11:30.067 --> 00:11:31.934
Trump was always so desperate
to buddy up with Putin,

00:11:31.934 --> 00:11:33.234
even Putin couldn't believe it.

00:11:33.234 --> 00:11:35.067
Trump was like those
rookie defensive backs

00:11:35.067 --> 00:11:37.267
who would stop Tom Brady
after the game for an autograph.

00:11:37.267 --> 00:11:39.033
"Hey, I know I'm on
the other team, but huge fan.

00:11:39.033 --> 00:11:40.834
Don't tell my coach."

00:11:40.834 --> 00:11:42.467
Putin always had
that smile on his face

00:11:42.467 --> 00:11:43.667
when he was next to Trump like,

00:11:43.667 --> 00:11:46.267
"I can't believe
how easy this is."

00:11:46.267 --> 00:11:47.701
And as much as I don't
want to hear

00:11:47.701 --> 00:11:49.767
from the Trumps
and Fox Newses of the world,

00:11:49.767 --> 00:11:51.868
I very much also
don't want to hear

00:11:51.868 --> 00:11:53.501
from the same
belligerent maniacs

00:11:53.501 --> 00:11:54.801
who have consistently been wrong

00:11:54.801 --> 00:11:56.300
about foreign policy
for decades,

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.400
like former Trump
national security adviser

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.567
and Bush administration
official John Bolton,

00:12:00.567 --> 00:12:03.400
one of the key cheerleaders
of the Iraq war

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.767
who has advocated for bombing
or invading multiple countries.

00:12:05.767 --> 00:12:08.033
For some reason, Bolton was
invited on MSNBC yesterday

00:12:08.033 --> 00:12:10.267
to give his take
on the Russia situation.

00:12:10.267 --> 00:12:11.734
-How do you deter
Vladimir Putin?

00:12:11.734 --> 00:12:15.467
He seems absolutely determined
to do what he is about to do,

00:12:15.467 --> 00:12:17.167
because he's amassed this force.

00:12:17.167 --> 00:12:18.601
Do you see him backing down?

00:12:18.601 --> 00:12:19.734
-I don't at this point.

00:12:19.734 --> 00:12:21.501
Look, the President
announced on Friday

00:12:21.501 --> 00:12:23.133
that his policy had failed.

00:12:23.133 --> 00:12:24.534
He said, unequivocally,

00:12:24.534 --> 00:12:27.601
the Russian decision
to invade Ukraine had been made.

00:12:27.601 --> 00:12:30.400
That's an admission
that deterrence has failed.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:33.133
-I'm sorry, but there's no one
I would rather hear from

00:12:33.133 --> 00:12:34.934
on foreign policy
less than John Bolton.

00:12:34.934 --> 00:12:36.667
I'm all for having experts
on cable news,

00:12:36.667 --> 00:12:37.934
but you don't get
to be an expert

00:12:37.934 --> 00:12:39.133
if you've never been right.

00:12:39.133 --> 00:12:41.367
Bolton was wrong on Iraq,
wrong on Afghanistan,

00:12:41.367 --> 00:12:43.067
wrong on the mustaches
coming back.

00:12:43.067 --> 00:12:45.367
Although I did
meet John Bolton once,

00:12:45.367 --> 00:12:47.400
and he told me
my Pacino impression is great.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.767
Oh [bleep]

00:12:48.767 --> 00:12:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:12:54.334 --> 00:12:57.267
That means it sucks, right?

00:12:57.267 --> 00:12:58.300
The leader
of the Republican Party

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.968
praised a bloodthirsty autocrat

00:12:59.968 --> 00:13:02.501
as the U.S. warns of an imminent
full-scale invasion

00:13:02.501 --> 00:13:04.968
that virtually the entire world
is horrified by.

00:13:04.968 --> 00:13:07.901
And yet the GOP has the gall
to call Biden weak.

00:13:07.901 --> 00:13:09.667
Maybe Trump
is just praising Putin

00:13:09.667 --> 00:13:12.701
in the hope that if he runs
again in 2024, Putin will say...

00:13:12.701 --> 00:13:14.501
-♪ Welcome back ♪

00:13:14.501 --> 00:13:16.901
[ Laughter ]

00:13:16.901 --> 00:13:18.300
-So I think in order
for that to work,

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:20.100
everybody here would have --

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:22.033
in the body
of the "Closer Look,"

00:13:22.033 --> 00:13:24.501
they would have had to leave and
go watch "Welcome Back, Kotter."

00:13:24.501 --> 00:13:26.334
[ Laughter ]

